     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 850\u20131,000 mg per dose. Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nCould the intended dose be one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg** per dose, in some other regimen\n\nTell me the correct dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is what you meant, please confirm that. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first, and I can add a note to the order documenting the rationale."
      }
     ],
